  1. Shift Request Intake                       
                                                                                                                                                                                  
  Parsing inbound requests (email/portal/phone), extracting structured data, triaging urgency. Currently unstructured — three channels, no standard format.                       
                                                                                                                                                                                  
  2. Candidate Matching                                                                                                                                                           
                                                                                                                                                                                  
  Selecting the right nurse given credentials, proximity, availability, hospital preferences, nurse preferences. The core cognitive load — 120 decisions/coordinator/day.         
  
  3. Credential & Compliance Verification                                                                                                                                         
                  
  License checks, background, training certs against state regulatory databases. Done manually today. Drives the 7% mismatch rate and creates async wait time.                    
  
  4. Availability Tracking                                                                                                                                                        
                  
  Maintaining an accurate real-time picture of nurse availability. Likely the most fragile workstream — the "Kim updates by hand" contradiction lives here.                       
  
  5. Outreach & Confirmation                                                                                                                                                      
                  
  Contacting nurses, getting shift confirmations, managing back-and-forth until a slot is filled. Major contributor to the 4.2h fill time.                                        
                  
  6. No-Show Response                                                                                                                                                             
                  
  Detecting no-shows, triggering emergency replacement workflows. 12% rate means this is high-frequency, time-critical, and currently reactive.                                   
                  
  7. Exception Handling & Escalation                                                                                                                                              
                  
  Non-standard cases: credential edge cases, hospital-specific requirements, urgent fills outside normal hours, VIP accounts. Volume unknown — this is a key probe target.        
                  
